  "verdict": "Position 401 (I) is VARIABLE in this set: the query residue occurs in 3.6 % of 332 de-duplicated homologs (98 genera) and Ser in 15.7 %; in the anchored subset (n=103) it is 6.8 % vs 39.8 % Ser. The catalytic control His537 reads 98.8 % on the same instrument (100.0 % anchored, Ser 0.0 %), so the instrument separates an invariant position from a variable one. The external MSA (Clustal Omega, 84 sequences) reads the same column as 10.7 % Ser / 3.6 % I with 61.9 % gaps: the direction agrees, the magnitudes do not, and the gap fraction is why — per sequence the two aligners agree on 33.3 % of the shared accessions, rising to 71.8 % once the cells where the external alignment places NO residue are excluded (45 of 84 cells). The external PAIRWISE alignments in the tree (EMBOSS Needle, n=8: Colletotrichum incanum → S; Gnomoniopsis smithogilvyi → S; Colletotrichum godetiae → S; Colletotrichum plurivorum → S; Colletotrichum shisoi → S; Colletotrichum sublineola → S; Colletotrichum navitas → S; Colletotrichum orchidophilum → S) agree with our reading in 8 of 8.",
